.It Track
The environment built so that failure stays survivable: sandbox, evaluation
environment, permissions, failure record, measurement.
.It Open day
Everyone on the same track, any vehicle, each driver on their own; the
current state of language model use.
.It Drivers never buy the track
The people who use infrastructure expect it to be perfect and do not fund
it; the people who fund it rarely see it used.
.It Crash history
The dated record of where things went wrong and what changed afterwards; the
track equivalent of a failure record.
.It Price ladder
The same infrastructure sold at different levels of support, from
pay-per-lap to a full team.
